JRBrown wrote:
> As far as I can tell, both random monsters and pets will avoid putting
> on cursed armor.

I'm not sure this is correct. Certainly pets don't pick up cursed 
objects (dogmove.c line 303) so naturally they won't wear anything 
cursed unless it was in their inventory when they became tame.

Things appear different for hostile and peaceful monsters. As far as I 
can see, the monster wear code - m_dowear() in worn.c - talkes no 
account of BUC status when deciding whether to wear something. It does 
prevent removal of cursed items, which happens silently for armour.

Similarly, in the pickup code for non-tame monsters - mpickstuff() in 
mon.c and mpickobj() in steal.c - there doesn't appear to be any 
consideration of the BUC status.

Getting monsters to pick stuff up in sight is harder than I expected; I 
finally managed a wizmode test however:

